A||||3||85seNUT||Cooling fan||||1||
Z||000000||85seNUT||02-17-2001||01:06 PM||||When i turn my car on, the cooling fan in the front goes on.  it is always on and i know that is not right.  Is there anyway to fix that?||||reg||1
Z||000001||WKDFIRO||02-17-2001||02:59 PM||||It might be that your temp sensor needs to be replaced. Is that 85 SE a four or a six?<P>The temp sensor acts as a ground. When the temperature reaches the predetermined level it will ground out the green w/white stripe wire and turn on the fan. If I remember correctly, when you take off the wire off of this sensor, the fan will go on automaticly as well. Also just make sure that your AC isn't always on too. The AC activates it as well.<P>Better the fan always come on than never at all! <P>Hope this helps a little.||||reg||1
Z||000002||William Federle||02-17-2001||03:04 PM||||Also, it might be that it is jumpered at the<BR>fan relay to be on all the time. Mine was when I got it. It was jumpered because the fan switch on the engine didn't work. My engine is an 84 duke - the fan switch on that car is the one on the drivers side end of the head that is screwed in horizantally pointing toward the front.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||02-17-2001||03:41 PM||||This definatly sounds like the fan contol line is tied to ground someplace..... You did shut off the AC controls didn't you? The AC turns on the fan....<P>The short could be intentional as mentioned above. Could be the fan switch. Could be bad AC controls. I think in some setups there is even an aditional switch in the AC system. ||||reg||1
